    "pressure": {
      "file": "oil_mist_lubrication_system_pressure.glb",
      "title": "A dry mist that condenses where it is needed",
      "description": "Compressed air through a venturi atomises oil into a very fine mist (≈ 1–3 µm) at a low header pressure (≈ 2–5 kPa). The mist travels without settling; at each bearing a reclassifier fitting (small orifice) makes the droplets coalesce so they wet the rolling elements. The slight positive pressure also keeps moisture and dust out of the housing. Oil use is very low and bearing life typically improves; drains and headers are sloped so condensed oil returns or is collected.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
